# THE LOCAL RUN WITH THE TWO REWARD CHANGES (user 2026-11-15: "do you recommend we stop and resume with reward
# changes?" -> "ok. do it").
# = slurm/local_frl_c0actor_privcritic_t01_ar2_keepgoal_nojx_fgx.env (Town01; goal kept fixed, no spawn in a
#   junction, release at 15,000, +100 at 200 m of explore, far own-town image in explore) with ONLY:
#   1. FRL_LANE_STEP_COST=0.1 instead of 0.5. MEASURED on c0 in the frozen phase at 0.5 (code 33c267f,
#      6,000 decisions): the lane cost was 0.47 a decision against about 0.6 of progress, so explore netted
#      +0.1 a decision -- driving on was worth almost nothing, and the 175,000-decision checkpoint ends every
#      deterministic explore episode on a crossing at ~20 m (c0: 260-310 m). At 0.1 the cost is ~0.09.
#      An earlier 0.1 run collapsed after its release, but it still had the moving-goal defect.
#   2. GOAL_MISS_END_M=10: a goal episode ends as a failure ("missed") once the car is 10 m further from the
#      goal than its closest. Goal mode netted -0.28 a decision on c0 even counting its +100 arrivals; a
#      missed goal was followed by up to 1,250 decisions of retreat charge and lane cost.
# WHAT TO READ FIRST, in the frozen phase (c0 driving): r_net_x and r_net_g clearly positive and q positive.
export FRL_LANE_STEP_COST=${FRL_LANE_STEP_COST:-0.1}
. "$REPO/slurm/local_frl_c0actor_privcritic_t01_ar2_keepgoal_nojx_fgx.env"
export GOAL_MISS_END_M=10
